WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.962
Each cell repeatedly interprets RNA instructions

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:08.645
through transfer RNA. Those small adapters constitute a

00:00:08.645 --> 00:00:10.401
complicated regulatory system.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.573
Before a protein takes shape, transfer RNA helps turn

00:00:19.573 --> 00:00:23.237
genetic instructions into an amino-acid sequence. It is

00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:25.069
not passive cellular plumbing.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.406
tRNA charging, chemical modification, cleavage and

00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:38.702
localisation create several different biological

00:00:38.702 --> 00:00:41.998
functions and possible intervention points.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.703
Aminoacyl-tRNA synthetases have catalytic charging

00:00:49.703 --> 00:00:54.256
functions, and some have additional signalling roles

00:00:54.256 --> 00:00:55.557
beyond translation.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:04.958
Disrupting universally needed translation can injure

00:01:04.958 --> 00:01:09.634
healthy cells. A drug programme must demonstrate a

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:10.803
disease-specific vulnerability.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.162
Charging, modification and recognition can be context

00:01:20.162 --> 00:01:23.874
dependent. A drug programme needs a specific

00:01:23.874 --> 00:01:27.585
dependency, not a general declaration about tRNA.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.915
An enzyme pocket, disease-associated RNA fragment or

00:01:36.915 --> 00:01:40.105
extracellular synthetase domain requires different

00:01:40.105 --> 00:01:42.657
chemistry, assays and delivery.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.338
Translation machinery is not automatically undruggable,

00:01:49.338 --> 00:01:53.670
and it is certainly not automatically safe to perturb.
